it('KERNEL-0349','rule','3.10','The §3.10 rows are the kernel part of the §5.3 invariant suite. Batch-local checks read only the commit record faces, its moved, promoted and demoted vertices, its changed and demoted edges and their one-ring, so a batch costs O(touched), never O(model) (SCL-1); whole-arena checks run at stage end, at save or in CI; the freeze check runs once per freeze and the pool check once per merge in O(overlay size). Class floors are the stages invariants, stated as §3.2 (2) says (GEO-35).',['§3.10 after table'],'kernel (suite §5.3)',['@CommitRecord'],['§5.3 invariant suite','§12 budgets'],['batch-local cost','SCL-1'])
it('KERNEL-0350','rule','3.10','Nesting admits no exception (J-A30.31): a passage under a building wing (item 30) is an L3 face of kind passage in one parent (§2.5 Passage, cut by S10 along one side line of the front plot, §4.6, §4.7 S10 (9), by splitFace or claimSubFace as any alley face); the wing overhead is a composition ring (§2.6), never a plat face, so no footprint straddles it and no level is crossed; the rear plots it serves carry their access rows on the edges they share with it, and §5.3 reachability walk crosses passage, alley and court faces through faceNeighbours (§3.4). A passage is never an L1 way (its L2 corridor would cut the footprint above and split the block; S10 never writes L1, §4.1).',['§3.10 Nesting admits no exception'],'kernel (Passage record §2.5; plot model §4.7 / V01, V02)',['§2.5 Passage','@splitFace','@claimSubFace','@faceNeighbours'],['§5.3 reachability walk','§4.7 S10 (9)'],['passage','J-A30.31'])
